  "principles": [
    "Relation identifiers and argument-role signatures are versioned infrastructure.",
    "Categorical argument values are source-derived strings, not per-source enums.",
    "Numeric values are copied from the same source Claim.",
    "Exactly the declared argument keys are permitted for each relation.",
    "No cross-Claim value resolution is allowed.",
    "Registry extension must be reviewed before exposure to a new blind benchmark Golden.",
    "Existing V2.4 relation signatures are not mutated; new generic relations are added when an old signature is domain-specific.",
    "Every argument role has a machine-readable semantic domain and grounding class.",
    "Study-purpose relations cannot be interpreted as biological results.",
    "Association-only relations cannot be upgraded to causality.",
    "Modal and interpretive epistemic classes must be preserved during evaluation.",
    "Generic increase/decrease relations do not imply gradual, rapid, or other kinetic rates."
  ],
